711:
(a) The city police department and code enforcement shall abate all nuisances resulting from violations of this article.
(b) Before issuance of a citation or taking any action to abate any such nuisance, the enforcement officials shall first make demand upon and give notice of the existence of a nuisance to the landowner or such persons or entities having the right to control such land in writing, requiring that the nuisance be abated within 30 days after service of the demand and notice.
(c) The notice shall be presented by both a physical posting on the property in the name of the landowner, or such persons or entities having a right to control the land, and by certified mail or statutory personal delivery to the landowner (as the owner's names and addresses are shown on the tax records of the county) or such persons or entities having a right to control the land. Notice shall be deemed complete and sufficient when so physically posted and personally delivered or mailed.
(d) The notice shall contain the following:
(1) Names and addresses of the owners of the property, according to the public records of the county;
(2) Location of the property on which the violation exists;
(3) A statement by the enforcement officer of enforcement officials that the property has been inspected pursuant to this section and that a violation of this section has been determined to exist on the property;
(4) A description of the existing nuisance;
(5) A requirement that the record owner of the property or such persons or entities having a right to control the land abate the nuisance within 30 days from the date of the notice.
(e) Each day that a violation of this section continues shall be considered a separate offense.
(f) Should the landowner or such persons or entities having the right to control such land not abate or correct the nuisance pursuant to the notice, the enforcement officials shall have the right to issue a citation for the violation of this section to the landowner or such persons or entities having the right to control such land.
(Ord. No. 05-2017-01, § 3, 5-1-2017; Ord. No. 10-2017-01, § 3, 10-2-2017)

